Q: Disable prefers-color-scheme: dark in django admin A: <p>I found that the way the theme toggling function is set up, Django ignores css-level color scheme manipulation this way. Noticing their <a href="https://github.com/django/django/blob/main/django/contrib/admin/static/admin/js/theme.js" rel="nofollow noreferrer">theme.js</a> code leverages localstorage, I tried just setting the theme variable to &quot;light&quot; and it works to lock it to light mode, ignoring browser / OS setting or changes. You'll also want to hide the theme toggle UI if you don't want users to use dark mode.</p>
<p>You can edit templates/admin/base_site.html like so:</p>
<pre><code>    
{% block extrastyle %}
    &lt;style&gt;
        .theme-toggle{
            display:none;
        }

    &lt;/style&gt;

    &lt;script&gt;
        localStorage.setItem(&quot;theme&quot;, &quot;light&quot;);
    &lt;/script&gt;

{% endblock %}
</code></pre>
<p>*** Keep in mind dark mode can be a relief for users with light sensitivity, so be sure to add implementing dark mode to your roadmap, and only use this for a short-term style fix</p>
